{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_superpowers_specs_2026_07_12_netis_scanning_ux_design", "label": "Scanning UX Design (C2)", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-12-netis-scanning-ux-design.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_superpowers_specs_2026_07_12_netis_scanning_ux_design_should_run_scan", "label": "shouldRunScan Manual-Bypass Guard", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-12-netis-scanning-ux-design.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "2-state scan model, no migration: scan_enabled now means periodic auto-scan; a manual Scan-now always works for any non-WireGuard subnet regardless of the flag (manual-only mode = auto off + click). The manual/auto distinction lives entirely in the scheduler, keyed off which select case fired, so the trigger channel carries no flag and Trigger's signature is unchanged. WireGuard subnets are never ARP-scannable."}, {"id": "docs_superpowers_specs_2026_07_12_netis_scanning_ux_design_toast_system", "label": "Toast Feedback System (#toasts, ScanToast)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-12-netis-scanning-ux-design.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The toast is 'started' feedback, not completion tracking \u2014 completion still flows through the existing SSE refresh which updates counts and the grid live. Buttons post with hx-target #toasts / hx-swap beforeend; toasts.js auto-dismisses and guards a missing container. The buffered trigger channel absorbs rapid clicks so no rate-limit UI."}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_superpowers_specs_2026_07_12_netis_scanning_ux_design", "target": "docs_superpowers_specs_2026_07_12_netis_scanning_ux_design_should_run_scan", "relation": "references",